=== SIGNATURE ===
label_lookup(arr,row_label,column_label)

=== COMMENT ===
Two-way lookup in a labelled 2D array: finds row_label in the first column and column_label in the first row and returns the value at their intersection.

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(arr, row_label, column_label,
   IFNA(
      INDEX(
         arr,
         XMATCH(z_scalar(row_label), INDEX(arr, , 1), 0),
         XMATCH(z_scalar(column_label), INDEX(arr, 1, ), 0)
      ),
      ""
   )
)

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Looks up a value in a labelled 2D table by row and column headers.

Arguments:
  arr          - a 2D array whose first column and first row hold the labels.
  row_label    - label to match in the first column.
  column_label - label to match in the first row.

Single-value arguments (flags, counts, delimiters, a single lookup value) may arrive as 1x1 arrays (TOCOL(x), {x}, a one-cell FILTER/INDEX result); they are collapsed to true scalars with z_scalar, so they behave exactly like the plain value.

Returns:
  The value at the intersection of the first matching row_label and column_label, or "" if either label is not found.

Example:
  label_lookup(tbl, "Mon", "Cost")
